<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 25.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 25.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended Jan 25</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   270	   1.36     433050 116.92    26.26</p>
<p>ITC		    385	   1.92     198800  76.54    26.00</p>
<p>Reliance	     255	   1.15     258950  66.03    23.52</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   190	   0.95     326350  62.01    26.07</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    335	   1.64     158850  53.21    25.53</p>
<p>MTNL		   240	   1.22     203300  48.79    26.51</p>
<p>ACC		   1335	   6.81	22200  29.64    26.60</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    235	   1.16     125400  29.47    25.74</p>
<p>Tata Power	   134	   0.67     191550  25.67    26.07</p>
<p>Bajaj Auto	   915	   2.35	27750  25.39    13.39</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 24.99 percent on an annualised basis against 38.15 percent in the previous carry forward account ended Jan 18.</p>
